{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.8,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U4", "U5"],
      "pins": ["U4.18", "U4.27", "U5.36", "U5.40"],
      "nets": ["ROW3"],
      "observed": "The ROW3 net contains U4 pin 18 (ROW3), U4 pin 27 (ROW7), U5 pin 36, and U5 pin 40.",
      "expected": "The specification requires five column and seven row keyboard lines, so ROW3 and ROW7 should be separate nets and the two SKW92A GPIOs should not be shorted together.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"48\") (name \"ROW3\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"27\") (pinfunction \"ROW7\")"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "netlist shows 5 column + 7 row lines wired directly to SKW92A GPIO pins"}
      ],
      "impact": "Keyboard rows 3 and 7 would be electrically merged, making keys in those rows indistinguishable during scanning; the shorted GPIOs could also contend if driven independently.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "Display_Power_Switch"],
      "observed": "C1 is specified in the netlist as 0.1uF/16V between GND and Display_Power_Switch.",
      "expected": "The EPD component table in the specification requires C1 to be 1 µF/25 V, like C5/C7/C8/C9/C10.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"0.1uF/16V\")"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V"}
      ],
      "impact": "The display power rail has less bulk decoupling than intended, increasing ripple/noise and potentially causing e-paper artifacts or boost-converter instability.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    },
    {
      "category": "footprint_mismatch",
      "components": ["C11"],
      "pins": ["C11.1", "C11.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C11-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C11 is a 0.1uF capacitor (libsource Device C) assigned an inductor footprint, with pin 1 on an unconnected net and pin 2 tied to GND.",
      "expected": "A capacitor should use a capacitor footprint, and if it is present as a bypass/decoupling part both terminals should connect to the intended rail and GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C11\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"58\") (name \"unconnected-(C11-Pad1)\")"}
      ],
      "impact": "If C11 was intended to decouple a supply, its open terminal means that bypass is missing; the inductor footprint may also be an assembly/source mismatch. If it is a dummy, the electrical effect is negligible.",
      "confidence": 0.34
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show at least one strong anomaly: the keyboard ROW3 net shorts ROW3 to ROW7 and two SKW92A GPIOs, contrary to the specified seven-row matrix. A lower-confidence but supported issue is C1's value mismatching the EPD specification, and C11 is an unconnected capacitor in an inductor footprint."
}

